=== D4. Einstein channels: which outputs can an equivariant map Curv -> Lambda^13 (x) g have? ===
  l: (mult of trivial, S^2_0, Weyl) in Lambda^1 (x) Lambda^l:
   0:(0,0,0); 1:(1,1,0); 2:(0,0,0); 3:(0,0,0); 4:(0,0,0); 5:(0,0,0); 6:(0,0,0); 7:(0,0,0); 8:(0,0,0); 9:(0,0,0); 10:(0,0,0); 11:(0,0,0); 12:(0,0,0); 13:(1,1,0); 14:(0,0,0)
  Weyl occurs in Lambda^1 (x) g for no l => every K-equivariant Shiab operator annihilates Weyl curvature; trivial and S^2_0 occur only for l in [1, 13]
  Hom(Lambda^3, Lambda^1 (x) Lambda^2) = 1;  Hom(Lambda^3, Lambda^2 (x) Lambda^13) = 1;  (Lambda^3)^K = 0
  self-adjoint Shiab operators restricted to so(7,8) x so(7,8): dim 1;  to so(8,8) x so(8,8): dim 2
